text	**#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  The README tells readers to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so that command fails. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  The take-in check did not return a clean `take #91`. It printed:  ``` #91: assigned to you #91: label in progress ```  The issue is already assigned to you and has the `in progress` label. No branch is linked to it, and no pull request exists. Another session of yours, on this computer or another one, may already be working on it.  **Is this work running somewhere else, or should it continue here?** If it is running elsewhere, I'll stop. If it should continue here, I'll create the branch `docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo` in a new worktree, fix the README, review the change and open the pull request.
person	It runs somewhere else.
text	Understood. I'm stopping here. #91 README: the install command says npm instal (the typo in the README's install command) stays with that other session. I made no branch, no worktree and no change, and the issue's assignee and `in progress` label are as they were.
