text	**#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  The README tells readers to run `npm instal shop`, which fails because npm has no `instal` command. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  I ran the check again, and nothing has changed since last time:  ``` #91: assigned to you #91: label in progress ```  No branch is linked and no pull request exists. Last time you said the work runs somewhere else, so I stopped.  **Does the work still run somewhere else, or should it continue here now?** If it continues here, I'll create `docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo` in a new worktree, fix the README, review the change and open the pull request. If it still runs elsewhere, I'll leave the issue as it is.
